WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.610
The Gulf of Mexico has a deep central basin and broad

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.350
shelves along parts of its margins.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.250
Florida and the Bahamas include shallow continental and carbonate-platform areas.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.010
In the Caribbean, the Lesser Antilles arc, trenches and the Cayman

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.070
transform system identify active boundaries.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.530
Different coastlines in this one region therefore record different crustal settings

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.270
and processes.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:27.730
During Jurassic breakup, extension thinned the continental margins and created restricted

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.070
basins in which sediment and salt accumulated.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.190
Later seafloor spreading opened the Gulf as Yucatan moved away from

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.350
the northern Gulf Coast. The inherited normal faults, continental shelves and

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.130
buried salt preserve that opening history even though the present Gulf

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.750
is not an active spreading basin.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:50.270
In the textbook's Cretaceous reconstruction, Gulf spreading stops while sedimentation continues.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.810
A thick basaltic oceanic plateau approaches from the Pacific, carried on

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.310
a plate bounded partly by transforms and led by a subduction

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.490
system and arc. The history is an interpretation assembled from evidence;

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:06.610
the source explicitly notes debate over whether all that plateau material

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.670
formed in the Pacific or locally.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:14.450
Atlantic oceanic lithosphere descends westward beneath the Caribbean at the Lesser

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.530
Antilles in the present-setting description.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.990
Another line later in the supplied section calls that slab east-dipping,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:25.930
creating an internal conflict. Keep the discrepancy visible rather than memorizing

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.810
both directions. The present map, trench position and overriding Caribbean plate

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.550
support the westward relationship used in this lesson.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Geologists combine on-land mapping, dated rock sequences, volcanic and fault locations,

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:43.230
seafloor surveys, seismic profiles and drilled samples.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:47.390
Paleomagnetic and spreading reconstructions supply wider plate context.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.070
The Cenozoic history also involves arc collision and continuing transform motion.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.770
A good explanation connects each proposed event to evidence and labels

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:59.590
unresolved alternatives, rather than treating a tidy sequence of colored maps

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.630
as direct observation.
